  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 521.02 Non-Renewal Upon Report",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-07-27",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 521.02 Non-Renewal Upon Report.\n\n(a) On receipt of a report from the commissioner of the department of transportation or their designee, indicating that the owner of a vehicle has evaded tolls or charges in violation of RSA 236:31, the director of motor vehicles shall forward a notice of non-renewal to such owner by first class mail.\n\n(b) The report in (a) above shall be submitted on official letterhead and include the following:\n\n(1) The unique identification number corresponding to the name and plate associated with a violation; and\n\n(2) The identity of the owner of the vehicle that has evaded tolls or charges.\n\n(c) The effective date of such non-renewal shall be 30 days subsequent to its issuance.\n\n(d) The notice of non-renewal shall include:\n\n(1) The reasons for the non-renewal order;\n\n(2) The effective date of the non-renewal and the authority therefor;\n\n(3) The administrative fine assessed;\n\n(4) A statement indicating that the owner may request an administrative hearing no later than 30 days from the date of the notice; and\n\n(5) Motor vehicle registration number.\n\nSource. #8544, eff 1-20-06; ss by #9372, INTERIM, eff 1-26-09, EXPIRES: 7-27-09; ss by #9487, eff 6-23-09; ss by #12426, eff 11-30-17 (formerly Saf-C 217.02) (See Revision Note at part heading for Saf-C 522); ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 522.02)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
